# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_resolve_qualified_tail_unique.py" "QUALIFIED-PATH TAIL UNIQUENESS GATE: PASS" "qualified-path leading-drop tail uniqueness" "qualified-path leading-drop (Rust/PHP) tail resolution requires a UNIQUE match — proven on a real-repo finding (symfony+laravel), not by inspection: the resolver's _candidates_bare qualified-path (::/\\) RECALL fallback dropped leading namespace segments and probed each multi-segment tail, but did 'cands |= sub; break' — it FANNED OUT to EVERY file matching the first non-empty tail. A 2-segment tail like Mapping/ClassMetadata is too generic in a large PSR-4 namespace and matches multiple unrelated files; the import that triggers the leading-drop is almost always an EXTERNAL class (a vendored Doctrine/Twig/Symfony class) that names NO internal file, so every fan-out target was a FALSE edge (symfony: use Doctrine\\Persistence\\Mapping\\ClassMetadata -> BOTH Serializer/Mapping + Validator/Mapping; laravel: use Symfony\\Component\\Console\\Application -> BOTH Illuminate/Console + Contracts/Console). Fix mirrors the Rust crate:: trailing-type fallback right below it (len(candidates)==1) + the Ruby bare-require uniqueness guard: accept a leading-drop tail ONLY when it resolves UNIQUELY; an ambiguous most-specific tail is suppressed. Recall-SAFE because the suffix index is monotone (a shorter tail's match set is a SUPERSET of any longer tail's, verified 0 violations on symfony+laravel) so an ambiguous tail can never disambiguate by shortening. Measured: symfony resolved_internal 31432->31014 (-418 false fan-out instances, 116 import-sites cleaned); laravel 8219->8193; ripgrep/tokio/vscode-Rust .rs-source edges byte-IDENTICAL (81/1681/127). This gate pins BOTH directions on a hermetic synthetic fixture: PRECISION (external ambiguous-tail import resolves to NEITHER same-tail file) and RECALL (a unique-tail PHP \\ import AND a unique Rust crate:: import STILL resolve). FAILS on pre-fix code (the false fan-out is present)." "qualified-path (::/\\) leading-drop tail must be UNIQUE to resolve — ambiguous same-tail fan-out (external Doctrine/Symfony classes -> N unrelated internal files) suppressed, unique recall preserved; Rust untouched (byte-identical on ripgrep/tokio)" 16
